xmodel/sol-xside.log-15564-+## 2. The x-side interface
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15565-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:15566:+### 2.1 Exact normalized factor streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15567-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15568-+For a genuine polynomial pair, take the y-leading polynomials
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15569-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15570-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15571-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15572-+ \phi_f(x)&=[y^{126}](f-a)
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15573-+   =c_f x^{42}+c_{f,41}x^{41}+\cdots+c_{f,0},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15574-+ \phi_g(x)&=[y^{189}]g
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15575-+   =c_g x^{63}+c_{g,62}x^{62}+\cdots+c_{g,0}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15576-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15577-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15578-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:15579:+The branch-product factorization in `SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md` gives the exact
xmodel/sol-xside.log:15580:+normalized, eta-independent factors
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15581-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15582-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15583-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15584-+ U_f(t)&=\frac{\phi_f(t^{-42})}{c_ft^{-1764}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15585-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{42}\alpha_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15586-+       &\alpha_m&=\frac{c_{f,42-m}}{c_f},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15587-+ U_g(t)&=\frac{\phi_g(t^{-42})}{c_gt^{-2646}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15588-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{63}\beta_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15589-+       &\beta_m&=\frac{c_{g,63-m}}{c_g}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15590-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.2}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15591-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15592-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:15593:+Thus the finite x-factor input sequences are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15594-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15595-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15596-+  (\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_{42}),\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15597-+  (\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_{63}),                              \tag{2.3}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15598-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15599-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:15600:+with factor-coordinate levels \(42m\). If
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15601-+\(\phi_f=c_f\prod_i(x-\xi_i)\) and
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15602-+\(\phi_g=c_g\prod_j(x-\zeta_j)\), then
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15603-+\(\alpha_1=-\sum_i\xi_i\) and \(\beta_1=-\sum_j\zeta_j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15604-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:15605:+D43 consumes only
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15606-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-15607-+\[
