xmodel/sol-xside.log-75494-+### 2.2 Mandatory tangent classification
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75495-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75496-+At a named completion, each consumed x coefficient must be classified as
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75497-+exactly one of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75498-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75499-+1. **held fixed:** its value is part of the completion and its differential
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75500-+   is excluded from the declared Newton source for a proved reason;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75501-+2. **derived:** it is an explicit function of the 30 y-tail streams, and the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75502-+   exact chain-rule row \(D\alpha,D\beta\) is supplied;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75503-+3. **independent:** it is a genuine filtered tangent coordinate.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75504-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:75505:+Cases 1 and 2 can preserve 180 columns. In case 3, D43 normally has two
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75506-+additional level-42 columns and shape \(184\times182\). Row 42 sees only one
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75507-+linear combination of them, but the other direction may engage later; it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75508-+cannot be quotiented away from a single-window kernel observation. A proved
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75509-+source quotient which retains only that combination would instead give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75510-+\(184\times181\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75511-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75512-+This classification is the load-bearing content of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75513-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75514-+> **CONJECTURE X-SIDE-30.** The level-42 x-side contributes no independent
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75515-+> source direction and no independent output stream outside the corrected
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75516-+> 30-by-30 model, after proved bridge/gauge relations.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75517-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75518-+If the classification is absent, the certifier must stop before constructing
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75519-+a loss matrix.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75520-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75521-+### 2.3 Causal structure
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75522-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:75523:+The normalized-factor convolution gives the following onset rules.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75524-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:75525:+| datum | assigned factor level | first possible residual level | first effect on a y-tail differential of level \(r\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-75526-+|---|---:|---:|---:|
