xmodel/sol-xside.log-77588-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77589-+ r_\rho=6+\rho\quad(\rho\ne4),\qquad r_4=16,\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77590-+ \sum_qr_q=288.                                             \tag{1.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77591-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77592-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77593-+The missing would-be shift \(r=10\) is `PIN42`: it pins the root-series
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77594-+coefficient of **absolute** level \(32+10=42\). It is not the normalized
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77595:+x-factor correction at **operator** level 42.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77596-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77597-+A coordinate `(family,r)` has global source level \(r\), absolute root-tail
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77598-+level \(32+r\), and belongs to the unique residue stream
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77599-+\(\rho\equiv r\pmod6\). In stream coordinates its \(j\)-th coefficient has
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77600-+level \(r_\rho+6j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77601-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77602-+### 1.2 The corrected 30 target streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77603-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77604-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77605-+ Y^+=\bigoplus_{a=0}^{29}t^{s_a}k[[u]]e_a,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77606-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77607-+
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77621-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77622-+**CONJECTURE CYCLIC-30.** These are all output streams at every depth.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77623-+Only the finite pure-y grading through band 41 is banked. At row 42 the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77624-+compiler must retain and audit every pristine eta component with \(a\ge30\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77625-+The slot-aware degree bound used by the present construction is
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77626-+\(\deg_\eta\Phi_y\le14\), \(\deg_\eta\Gamma_y\le20\) through \(t^{42}\),
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77627-+so the possible surplus is eta 30--33; that bound itself must be established
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77628-+before truncation. A new independent component enlarges the target; it may
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77629-+not be discarded because it misses the 30-stream selector.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77630-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77631-+## 2. The x-side interface
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77632-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77633:+### 2.1 Exact normalized factor streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77634-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77635-+For a genuine polynomial pair, take the y-leading polynomials
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77636-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77637-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77638-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77639-+ \phi_f(x)&=[y^{126}](f-a)
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77640-+   =c_f x^{42}+c_{f,41}x^{41}+\cdots+c_{f,0},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77641-+ \phi_g(x)&=[y^{189}]g
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77642-+   =c_g x^{63}+c_{g,62}x^{62}+\cdots+c_{g,0}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77643-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77644-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77645-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77646:+The branch-product factorization in `SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md` gives the exact
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77647:+normalized, eta-independent factors
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77648-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77649-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77650-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77651-+ U_f(t)&=\frac{\phi_f(t^{-42})}{c_ft^{-1764}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77652-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{42}\alpha_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77653-+       &\alpha_m&=\frac{c_{f,42-m}}{c_f},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77654-+ U_g(t)&=\frac{\phi_g(t^{-42})}{c_gt^{-2646}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77655-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{63}\beta_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77656-+       &\beta_m&=\frac{c_{g,63-m}}{c_g}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77657-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.2}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77658-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77659-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77660:+Thus the finite x-factor input sequences are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77661-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77662-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77663-+  (\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_{42}),\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77664-+  (\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_{63}),                              \tag{2.3}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77665-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77666-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77667:+with factor-coordinate levels \(42m\). If
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77668-+\(\phi_f=c_f\prod_i(x-\xi_i)\) and
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77669-+\(\phi_g=c_g\prod_j(x-\zeta_j)\), then
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77670-+\(\alpha_1=-\sum_i\xi_i\) and \(\beta_1=-\sum_j\zeta_j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77671-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77672:+The D43 Euler/J window directly consumes only
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77673-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77674-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77675-+       \alpha:=\alpha_1,\qquad \beta:=\beta_1,\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77676-+       U_f=1+\alpha t^{42}+O(t^{84}),\quad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77677-+       U_g=1+\beta t^{42}+O(t^{84}).                        \tag{2.4}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77678-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77679-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77680-+These sequences are not six-step \(k[[u]]\) tail streams. They are finite
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77681:+sparse factor coordinates supported at \(42m=7m\) powers of \(u\). Unless a
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77682-+proved bridge expresses them in the 30 streams, an implementation should
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77683-+represent their tangent directions as a sparse x-side column sidecar.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77684-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77685-+**CONJECTURE X-SIDE-DERIVATION.** The pending LR2/R2 x-side model derives
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77686-+the values and tangent maps of (2.3), with all its h-Newton budget equations,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77687-+from legal polynomial/source data. LR2 proves the single-cluster geometry;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77688-+it does not supply these coefficients or their Jacobian. `SHEET6-R1.md`
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77689-+section 16.5 explicitly records this model as future work.
