xmodel/sol-xside.log-77691-+### 2.2 Mandatory tangent classification
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77692-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77693-+At a named completion, each consumed x coefficient must be classified as
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77694-+exactly one of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77695-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77696-+1. **held fixed:** its value is part of the completion and its differential
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77697-+   is excluded from the declared Newton source for a proved reason;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77698-+2. **derived:** it is an explicit function of the 30 y-tail streams, and the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77699-+   exact chain-rule row \(D\alpha,D\beta\) is supplied;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77700-+3. **independent:** it is a genuine filtered tangent coordinate.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77701-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:77702:+Cases 1 and 2 can preserve 180 columns. In case 3, D43 normally has two
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77703-+additional level-42 columns and shape \(184\times182\). Row 42 sees only one
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77704-+linear combination of them, but the other direction may engage later; it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77705-+cannot be quotiented away from a single-window kernel observation. A proved
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77706-+source quotient which retains only that combination would instead give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77707-+\(184\times181\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77708-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77709-+This classification is the load-bearing content of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77710-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77711-+> **CONJECTURE X-SIDE-30.** The level-42 x-side contributes no independent
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77712-+> source direction and no independent output stream outside the corrected
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77713-+> 30-by-30 model, after proved bridge/gauge relations.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77714-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77715-+If the classification is absent, the certifier must stop before constructing
xmodel/sol-xside.log-77716-+a loss matrix.
