xmodel/sol-xside.log-78664-+## 1. Corrected source and target coordinates
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78665-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78666-+### 1.1 The banked 30 y-tail input streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78667-+
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78682-+| 25--27 | `tg01` | \(0,2,4\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78683-+| 28--30 | `tg02` | \(0,2,4\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78684-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78685-+Their shifts are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78686-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78687-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78688-+ r_\rho=6+\rho\quad(\rho\ne4),\qquad r_4=16,\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78689-+ \sum_qr_q=288.                                             \tag{1.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78690-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78691-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78692-+The missing would-be shift \(r=10\) is `PIN42`: it pins the root-series
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78693-+coefficient of **absolute** level \(32+10=42\). It is not the normalized
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78694:+x-factor correction at **operator** level 42.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78695-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78696-+A coordinate `(family,r)` has global source level \(r\), absolute root-tail
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78697-+level \(32+r\), and belongs to the unique residue stream
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78698-+\(\rho\equiv r\pmod6\). In stream coordinates its \(j\)-th coefficient has
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78699-+level \(r_\rho+6j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78700-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78701-+### 1.2 The corrected 30 target streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78702-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78703-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78704-+ Y^+=\bigoplus_{a=0}^{29}t^{s_a}k[[u]]e_a,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78705-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78706-+
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78720-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78721-+**CONJECTURE CYCLIC-30.** These are all output streams at every depth.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78722-+Only the finite pure-y grading through band 41 is banked. At row 42 the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78723-+compiler must retain and audit every pristine eta component with \(a\ge30\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78724-+The slot-aware degree bound used by the present construction is
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78725-+\(\deg_\eta\Phi_y\le14\), \(\deg_\eta\Gamma_y\le20\) through \(t^{42}\),
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78726-+so the possible surplus is eta 30--33; that bound itself must be established
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78727-+before truncation. A new independent component enlarges the target; it may
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78728-+not be discarded because it misses the 30-stream selector.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78729-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78730-+## 2. The x-side interface
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78731-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78732:+### 2.1 Exact normalized factor streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78733-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78734-+For a genuine polynomial pair, take the y-leading polynomials
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78735-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78736-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78737-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78738-+ \phi_f(x)&=[y^{126}](f-a)
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78739-+   =c_f x^{42}+c_{f,41}x^{41}+\cdots+c_{f,0},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78740-+ \phi_g(x)&=[y^{189}]g
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78741-+   =c_g x^{63}+c_{g,62}x^{62}+\cdots+c_{g,0}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78742-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78743-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78744-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78745:+The branch-product factorization in `SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md` gives the exact
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78746:+normalized, eta-independent factors
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78747-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78748-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78749-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78750-+ U_f(t)&=\frac{\phi_f(t^{-42})}{c_ft^{-1764}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78751-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{42}\alpha_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78752-+       &\alpha_m&=\frac{c_{f,42-m}}{c_f},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78753-+ U_g(t)&=\frac{\phi_g(t^{-42})}{c_gt^{-2646}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78754-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{63}\beta_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78755-+       &\beta_m&=\frac{c_{g,63-m}}{c_g}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78756-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.2}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78757-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78758-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78759:+Thus the finite x-factor input sequences are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78760-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78761-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78762-+  (\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_{42}),\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78763-+  (\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_{63}),                              \tag{2.3}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78764-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78765-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78766:+with factor-coordinate levels \(42m\). If
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78767-+\(\phi_f=c_f\prod_i(x-\xi_i)\) and
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78768-+\(\phi_g=c_g\prod_j(x-\zeta_j)\), then
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78769-+\(\alpha_1=-\sum_i\xi_i\) and \(\beta_1=-\sum_j\zeta_j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78770-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78771:+The D43 Euler/J window directly consumes only
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78772-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78773-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78774-+       \alpha:=\alpha_1,\qquad \beta:=\beta_1,\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78775-+       U_f=1+\alpha t^{42}+O(t^{84}),\quad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78776-+       U_g=1+\beta t^{42}+O(t^{84}).                        \tag{2.4}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78777-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78778-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78779-+These sequences are not six-step \(k[[u]]\) tail streams. They are finite
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78780:+sparse factor coordinates supported at \(42m=7m\) powers of \(u\). Unless a
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78781-+proved bridge expresses them in the 30 streams, an implementation should
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78782-+represent their tangent directions as a sparse x-side column sidecar.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78783-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78784-+**CONJECTURE X-SIDE-DERIVATION.** The pending LR2/R2 x-side model derives
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78785-+the values and tangent maps of (2.3), with all its h-Newton budget equations,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78786-+from legal polynomial/source data. LR2 proves the single-cluster geometry;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78787-+it does not supply these coefficients or their Jacobian. `SHEET6-R1.md`
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78788-+section 16.5 explicitly records this model as future work.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78789-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78790-+### 2.2 Mandatory tangent classification
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78791-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78792-+At a named completion, each consumed x coefficient must be classified as
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78793-+exactly one of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78794-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78795-+1. **held fixed:** its value is part of the completion and its differential
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78796-+   is excluded from the declared Newton source for a proved reason;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78797-+2. **derived:** it is an explicit function of the 30 y-tail streams, and the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78798-+   exact chain-rule row \(D\alpha,D\beta\) is supplied;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78799-+3. **independent:** it is a genuine filtered tangent coordinate.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78800-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78801:+Cases 1 and 2 can preserve 180 columns. In case 3, D43 normally has two
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78802-+additional level-42 columns and shape \(184\times182\). Row 42 sees only one
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78803-+linear combination of them, but the other direction may engage later; it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78804-+cannot be quotiented away from a single-window kernel observation. A proved
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78805-+source quotient which retains only that combination would instead give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78806-+\(184\times181\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78807-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78808-+This classification is the load-bearing content of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78809-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78810-+> **CONJECTURE X-SIDE-30.** The level-42 x-side contributes no independent
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78811-+> source direction and no independent output stream outside the corrected
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78812-+> 30-by-30 model, after proved bridge/gauge relations.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78813-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78814-+If the classification is absent, the certifier must stop before constructing
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78815-+a loss matrix.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78816-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78817-+### 2.3 Causal structure
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78818-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78819:+The normalized-factor convolution gives the following onset rules.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78820-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:78821:+| datum | assigned factor level | first possible residual level | first effect on a y-tail differential of level \(r\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78822-+|---|---:|---:|---:|
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78823-+| value \(\alpha_m\) or \(\beta_m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m+r\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78824-+| independent \(D\alpha_m\) or \(D\beta_m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78825-+| product \(\alpha_i\beta_j\) | \(42(i+j)\) | \(42(i+j)\) | later by convolution |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78826-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78827-+Consequences for the band-42 window:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78828-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78829-+- only \(\alpha,\beta\) can affect the residual value;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78830-+- if \(\alpha,\beta\) are held fixed, their multiplication of a registered
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78831-+  y-tail variation starts at \(42+6=48\), so it does not alter the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78832-+  30-tail derivative through row 42;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78833-+- if they are derived, \(D\alpha,D\beta\) add a chain-rule contribution at
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78990-+    +252S_MG_M(3\alpha-2\beta)\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78991-+  &=h^{\,y}_{29,1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78992-+    -\frac{9\,7^{31}}{2^{13}}(3\alpha-2\beta).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78993-+\end{aligned}}                                             \tag{3.9}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78994-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78995-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78996-+There is no honest numerical specialization of (3.9) in the current
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78997-+repository because \(\alpha,\beta\) are not banked. Assigning them zero is
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78998-+only a constructor/control assignment. It becomes a legal named completion
xmodel/sol-xside.log-78999-+only if exact polynomial or LR2/R2 provenance proves that those zero values
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79000-+belong to the scoped source scheme.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79001-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79002:+At a genuine D43 survivor, (3.9) must evaluate to zero as a residual row.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79003-+The loss test concerns the derivative row and the unit codomain target
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79004-+\(t^{42}e_{29}\); it does not treat the residual value itself as the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79005-+obstruction.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79006-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79007-+In the existing held-lead tails tangent convention,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79008-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79009-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79010-+ D([u^1]H_{29})
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79011-+  =Dh^{\,y}_{29,1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79012-+   +252S_MG_M(3D\alpha-2D\beta).                            \tag{3.10}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79013-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79014-+
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79098-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79099-+Equation (4.2) is conditional. Independent \(\alpha,\beta\) give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79100-+\(184\times182\); a proved one-coordinate x quotient gives
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79101-+\(184\times181\); any surplus output adds rows.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79102-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79103-+For artifact stability, define the canonical serialized order to be:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79104-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79105-+1. the exact old ordered row registry, followed by the ten new rows in the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79106-+   order printed above;
