xmodel/sol-xside.log-79829-+## 2. The x-side interface
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79830-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79831:+### 2.1 Exact normalized factor streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79832-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79833-+For a genuine polynomial pair, take the y-leading polynomials
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79834-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79835-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79836-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79837-+ \phi_f(x)&=[y^{126}](f-a)
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79838-+   =c_f x^{42}+c_{f,41}x^{41}+\cdots+c_{f,0},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79839-+ \phi_g(x)&=[y^{189}]g
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79840-+   =c_g x^{63}+c_{g,62}x^{62}+\cdots+c_{g,0}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79841-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79842-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79843-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79844:+The branch-product factorization in `SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md` gives the exact
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79845:+normalized, eta-independent factors
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79846-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79847-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79848-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79849-+ U_f(t)&=\frac{\phi_f(t^{-42})}{c_ft^{-1764}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79850-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{42}\alpha_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79851-+       &\alpha_m&=\frac{c_{f,42-m}}{c_f},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79852-+ U_g(t)&=\frac{\phi_g(t^{-42})}{c_gt^{-2646}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79853-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{63}\beta_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79854-+       &\beta_m&=\frac{c_{g,63-m}}{c_g}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79855-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.2}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79856-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79857-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79858:+Thus the finite x-factor input sequences are
