xmodel/sol-xside.log-79889-+### 2.2 Mandatory tangent classification
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79890-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79891-+At a named completion, each consumed x coefficient must be classified as
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79892-+exactly one of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79893-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79894-+1. **held fixed:** its value is part of the completion and its differential
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79895-+   is excluded from the declared Newton source for a proved reason;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79896-+2. **derived:** it is an explicit function of the 30 y-tail streams, and the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79897-+   exact chain-rule row \(D\alpha,D\beta\) is supplied;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79898-+3. **independent:** it is a genuine filtered tangent coordinate.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79899-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79900:+Cases 1 and 2 can preserve 180 columns. In case 3, D43 normally has two
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79901-+additional level-42 columns and shape \(184\times182\). Row 42 sees only one
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79902-+linear combination of them, but the other direction may engage later; it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79903-+cannot be quotiented away from a single-window kernel observation. A proved
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79904-+source quotient which retains only that combination would instead give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79905-+\(184\times181\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79906-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79907-+This classification is the load-bearing content of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79908-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79909-+> **CONJECTURE X-SIDE-30.** The level-42 x-side contributes no independent
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79910-+> source direction and no independent output stream outside the corrected
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79911-+> 30-by-30 model, after proved bridge/gauge relations.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79912-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79913-+If the classification is absent, the certifier must stop before constructing
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79914-+a loss matrix.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79915-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79916-+### 2.3 Causal structure
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79917-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79918:+The normalized-factor convolution gives the following onset rules.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-79919-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:79920:+| datum | assigned factor level | first possible residual level | first effect on a y-tail differential of level \(r\) |
