xmodel/sol-xside.log:82411:+### 2.1 Exact normalized factor streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82412-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82413-+For a genuine polynomial pair, take the y-leading polynomials
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82414-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82415-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82416-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82417-+ \phi_f(x)&=[y^{126}](f-a)
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82418-+   =c_f x^{42}+c_{f,41}x^{41}+\cdots+c_{f,0},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82419-+ \phi_g(x)&=[y^{189}]g
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82420-+   =c_g x^{63}+c_{g,62}x^{62}+\cdots+c_{g,0}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82421-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82422-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82423-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:82424:+The branch-product factorization in `SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md` gives the exact
xmodel/sol-xside.log:82425:+normalized, eta-independent factors
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82426-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82427-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82428-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82429-+ U_f(t)&=\frac{\phi_f(t^{-42})}{c_ft^{-1764}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82430-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{42}\alpha_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82431-+       &\alpha_m&=\frac{c_{f,42-m}}{c_f},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82432-+ U_g(t)&=\frac{\phi_g(t^{-42})}{c_gt^{-2646}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82433-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{63}\beta_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82434-+       &\beta_m&=\frac{c_{g,63-m}}{c_g}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82435-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.2}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82436-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82437-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:82438:+Thus the finite x-factor input sequences are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82439-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82440-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82441-+  (\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_{42}),\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82442-+  (\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_{63}),                              \tag{2.3}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82443-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82444-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:82445:+with factor-coordinate levels \(42m\). If
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82446-+\(\phi_f=c_f\prod_i(x-\xi_i)\) and
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82447-+\(\phi_g=c_g\prod_j(x-\zeta_j)\), then
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82448-+\(\alpha_1=-\sum_i\xi_i\) and \(\beta_1=-\sum_j\zeta_j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-82449-+
