xmodel/sol-xside.log-84723-+### 2.2 Mandatory tangent classification
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84724-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84725-+At a named completion, each consumed x coefficient must be classified as
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84726-+exactly one of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84727-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84728-+1. **held fixed:** its value is part of the completion and its differential
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84729-+   is excluded from the declared Newton source for a proved reason;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84730-+2. **derived:** it is an explicit function of the 30 y-tail streams, and the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84731-+   exact chain-rule row \(D\alpha,D\beta\) is supplied;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84732-+3. **independent:** it is a genuine filtered tangent coordinate.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84733-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:84734:+Cases 1 and 2 can preserve 180 columns. In case 3, D43 normally has two
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84735-+additional level-42 columns and shape \(184\times182\). Row 42 sees only one
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84736-+linear combination of them, but the other direction may engage later; it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84737-+cannot be quotiented away from a single-window kernel observation. A proved
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84738-+source quotient which retains only that combination would instead give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84739-+\(184\times181\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84740-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84741-+This classification is the load-bearing content of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84742-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84743-+> **CONJECTURE X-SIDE-30.** The level-42 x-side contributes no independent
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84744-+> source direction and no independent output stream outside the corrected
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84745-+> 30-by-30 model, after proved bridge/gauge relations.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84746-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84747-+If the classification is absent, the certifier must stop before constructing
xmodel/sol-xside.log-84748-+a loss matrix.
