xmodel/sol-xside.log-85712-+## 1. Corrected source and target coordinates
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85713-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85714-+### 1.1 The banked 30 y-tail input streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85715-+
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85730-+| 25--27 | `tg01` | \(0,2,4\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85731-+| 28--30 | `tg02` | \(0,2,4\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85732-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85733-+Their shifts are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85734-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85735-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85736-+ r_\rho=6+\rho\quad(\rho\ne4),\qquad r_4=16,\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85737-+ \sum_qr_q=288.                                             \tag{1.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85738-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85739-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85740-+The missing would-be shift \(r=10\) is `PIN42`: it pins the root-series
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85741-+coefficient of **absolute** level \(32+10=42\). It is not the normalized
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85742:+x-factor correction at **operator** level 42.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85743-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85744-+A coordinate `(family,r)` has global source level \(r\), absolute root-tail
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85745-+level \(32+r\), and belongs to the unique residue stream
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85746-+\(\rho\equiv r\pmod6\). In stream coordinates its \(j\)-th coefficient has
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85747-+level \(r_\rho+6j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85748-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85749-+### 1.2 The corrected 30 target streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85750-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85751-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85752-+ Y^+=\bigoplus_{a=0}^{29}t^{s_a}k[[u]]e_a,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85753-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85754-+
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85768-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85769-+**CONJECTURE CYCLIC-30.** These are all output streams at every depth.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85770-+Only the finite pure-y grading through band 41 is banked. At row 42 the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85771-+compiler must retain and audit every pristine eta component with \(a\ge30\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85772-+The slot-aware degree bound used by the present construction is
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85773-+\(\deg_\eta\Phi_y\le14\), \(\deg_\eta\Gamma_y\le20\) through \(t^{42}\),
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85774-+so the possible surplus is eta 30--33; that bound itself must be established
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85775-+before truncation. A new independent component enlarges the target; it may
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85776-+not be discarded because it misses the 30-stream selector.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85777-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85778-+## 2. The x-side interface
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85779-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85780:+### 2.1 Exact normalized factor streams
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85781-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85782-+For a genuine polynomial pair, take the y-leading polynomials
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85783-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85784-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85785-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85786-+ \phi_f(x)&=[y^{126}](f-a)
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85787-+   =c_f x^{42}+c_{f,41}x^{41}+\cdots+c_{f,0},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85788-+ \phi_g(x)&=[y^{189}]g
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85789-+   =c_g x^{63}+c_{g,62}x^{62}+\cdots+c_{g,0}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85790-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85791-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85792-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85793:+The branch-product factorization in `SHEET6-DIRECTIONB.md` gives the exact
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85794:+normalized, eta-independent factors
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85795-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85796-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85797-+\begin{aligned}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85798-+ U_f(t)&=\frac{\phi_f(t^{-42})}{c_ft^{-1764}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85799-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{42}\alpha_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85800-+       &\alpha_m&=\frac{c_{f,42-m}}{c_f},\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85801-+ U_g(t)&=\frac{\phi_g(t^{-42})}{c_gt^{-2646}}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85802-+       =1+\sum_{m=1}^{63}\beta_m t^{42m},
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85803-+       &\beta_m&=\frac{c_{g,63-m}}{c_g}.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85804-+\end{aligned}                                               \tag{2.2}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85805-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85806-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85807:+Thus the finite x-factor input sequences are
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85808-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85809-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85810-+  (\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_{42}),\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85811-+  (\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_{63}),                              \tag{2.3}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85812-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85813-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85814:+with factor-coordinate levels \(42m\). If
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85815-+\(\phi_f=c_f\prod_i(x-\xi_i)\) and
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85816-+\(\phi_g=c_g\prod_j(x-\zeta_j)\), then
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85817-+\(\alpha_1=-\sum_i\xi_i\) and \(\beta_1=-\sum_j\zeta_j\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85818-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85819:+The D43 Euler/J window directly consumes only
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85820-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85821-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85822-+       \alpha:=\alpha_1,\qquad \beta:=\beta_1,\qquad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85823-+       U_f=1+\alpha t^{42}+O(t^{84}),\quad
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85824-+       U_g=1+\beta t^{42}+O(t^{84}).                        \tag{2.4}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85825-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85826-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85827-+These sequences are not six-step \(k[[u]]\) tail streams. They are finite
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85828:+sparse factor coordinates supported at \(42m=7m\) powers of \(u\). Unless a
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85829-+proved bridge expresses them in the 30 streams, an implementation should
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85830-+represent their tangent directions as a sparse x-side column sidecar.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85831-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85832-+**CONJECTURE X-SIDE-DERIVATION.** The pending LR2/R2 x-side model derives
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85833-+the values and tangent maps of (2.3), with all its h-Newton budget equations,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85834-+from legal polynomial/source data. LR2 proves the single-cluster geometry;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85835-+it does not supply these coefficients or their Jacobian. `SHEET6-R1.md`
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85836-+section 16.5 explicitly records this model as future work.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85837-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85838-+### 2.2 Mandatory tangent classification
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85839-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85840-+At a named completion, each consumed x coefficient must be classified as
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85841-+exactly one of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85842-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85843-+1. **held fixed:** its value is part of the completion and its differential
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85844-+   is excluded from the declared Newton source for a proved reason;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85845-+2. **derived:** it is an explicit function of the 30 y-tail streams, and the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85846-+   exact chain-rule row \(D\alpha,D\beta\) is supplied;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85847-+3. **independent:** it is a genuine filtered tangent coordinate.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85848-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85849:+Cases 1 and 2 can preserve 180 columns. In case 3, D43 normally has two
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85850-+additional level-42 columns and shape \(184\times182\). Row 42 sees only one
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85851-+linear combination of them, but the other direction may engage later; it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85852-+cannot be quotiented away from a single-window kernel observation. A proved
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85853-+source quotient which retains only that combination would instead give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85854-+\(184\times181\).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85855-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85856-+This classification is the load-bearing content of:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85857-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85858-+> **CONJECTURE X-SIDE-30.** The level-42 x-side contributes no independent
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85859-+> source direction and no independent output stream outside the corrected
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85860-+> 30-by-30 model, after proved bridge/gauge relations.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85861-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85862-+If the classification is absent, the certifier must stop before constructing
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85863-+a loss matrix.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85864-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85865-+### 2.3 Causal structure
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85866-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85867:+The normalized-factor convolution gives the following onset rules.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85868-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:85869:+| datum | assigned factor level | first possible residual level | first effect on a y-tail differential of level \(r\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85870-+|---|---:|---:|---:|
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85871-+| value \(\alpha_m\) or \(\beta_m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m+r\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85872-+| independent \(D\alpha_m\) or \(D\beta_m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m\) | \(42m\) |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85873-+| product \(\alpha_i\beta_j\) | \(42(i+j)\) | \(42(i+j)\) | later by convolution |
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85874-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85875-+Consequences for the band-42 window:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85876-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85877-+- only \(\alpha,\beta\) can affect the residual value;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85878-+- if \(\alpha,\beta\) are held fixed, their multiplication of a registered
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85879-+  y-tail variation starts at \(42+6=48\), so it does not alter the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85880-+  30-tail derivative through row 42;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-85881-+- if they are derived, \(D\alpha,D\beta\) add a chain-rule contribution at
--
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86038-+    +252S_MG_M(3\alpha-2\beta)\\
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86039-+  &=h^{\,y}_{29,1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86040-+    -\frac{9\,7^{31}}{2^{13}}(3\alpha-2\beta).
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86041-+\end{aligned}}                                             \tag{3.9}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86042-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86043-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86044-+There is no honest numerical specialization of (3.9) in the current
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86045-+repository because \(\alpha,\beta\) are not banked. Assigning them zero is
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86046-+only a constructor/control assignment. It becomes a legal named completion
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86047-+only if exact polynomial or LR2/R2 provenance proves that those zero values
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86048-+belong to the scoped source scheme.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86049-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log:86050:+At a genuine D43 survivor, (3.9) must evaluate to zero as a residual row.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86051-+The loss test concerns the derivative row and the unit codomain target
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86052-+\(t^{42}e_{29}\); it does not treat the residual value itself as the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86053-+obstruction.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86054-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86055-+In the existing held-lead tails tangent convention,
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86056-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86057-+\[
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86058-+ D([u^1]H_{29})
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86059-+  =Dh^{\,y}_{29,1}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86060-+   +252S_MG_M(3D\alpha-2D\beta).                            \tag{3.10}
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86061-+\]
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86062-+
