xmodel/sol-xside.log-86146-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86147-+Equation (4.2) is conditional. Independent \(\alpha,\beta\) give
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86148-+\(184\times182\); a proved one-coordinate x quotient gives
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86149-+\(184\times181\); any surplus output adds rows.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86150-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86151-+For artifact stability, define the canonical serialized order to be:
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86152-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86153-+1. the exact old ordered row registry, followed by the ten new rows in the
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86154-+   order printed above;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86155-+2. the exact old ordered `GIDX` column registry, followed by the ten new
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86156-+   columns in the order printed above;
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86157-+3. any proved independent x-side columns after those, ordered by
xmodel/sol-xside.log:86158:+   `(factor, m)`.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86159-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86160-+The current a-major/family-major comprehensions would insert new labels
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86161-+inside the old lists. An internal implementation may use that order, but it
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86162-+must project and reorder by stable labels before hashing. A naïve top-left
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86163-+slice is not an acceptable legacy gate unless the append-only serialization
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86164-+above has first been enforced.
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86165-+
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86166-+### 4.2 Do not conflate three matrices
xmodel/sol-xside.log-86167-+
